    {
      "id": 219812,
      "name": "dpt",
      "username": "dpt",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-07-16T14:01:40.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Oops, I've been doing that Event wrong this whole time, then - is the \"Coastal Lands don't count\" thing mentioned in the rulebook somewhere? I feel like I would've noticed it at some point if it was…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>\"Coastal Lands don't count\" is just a shorthand. There are 4 terrain types (Mountain, Sands, Jungle, and Wetlands), as explained on p. 13 of the base game rulebook. \"Coastal\" and \"Inland\" are adjectives that apply to certain lands, but are not terrain types themselves. The Event card says to do something paying attention to terrain types on cards, and \"Coastal\" is not a terrain type, so doesn't affect the Event.</p>",
      "post_number": 10,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:52:11.808Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
