      "id": 219813,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-07-16T15:22:32.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>FYI: Per the Glossary from the rulebook:&nbsp;</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Spirit Island rulebook\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Spirit Island rulebook:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Land Type: A description of what sort of land to act upon. This may be a terrain, Coastal/Inland, or a requirement for what’s in/not in the land (e.g. “A land with Invaders”). [p. 13, 16]</p>\n<p>…</p>\n<p>Terrain: Jungle, Mountain, Sands, or Wetland. Each land has one terrain. [p. 13]</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>So \"Coastal\" is a <em>Land Type</em>, but not a <em>Terrain Type</em>, whereas \"Jungle\" is both.</p>\n<p>That's my take, anyway.&nbsp; <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:52:11.925Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
